    "id": "overlap-pilot",
    "language": "In soccer, we often find ourselves in two v ones. (breaths in) How do we convert these two v one situations into a goal? It's very simple. Your opponent with the ball approaches the defending player, drawing him out and may- forcing the defender to- to close him down. This cancels out these two players, turning the two v one into a one v zero, giving me the opportunity to run into the space to the side and having an open goal to shoot. Here I run. I receive the ball. However, in this scenario, the defender has cl- has closed me off. I have no option to score. So our- our other teammate now has the opportunity to score in a better space, and so I will give the ball back to him. And now he will have the opportunity to score on an a- open goal. So here in this situation, despite the fact that the defender was quick and was able to shut us down, we still get the ball back to our teammate, giving him the opportunity to still score.",
